condition has broad implications in the over-
all health of these patients. Our case shows
that rhabdomyolysis with extremely elevated
CPK can be seen in SPS, which can lead to
medical complications such as renal failure,
leukocytosis, and pulmonary edema. Early
diagnosis and management of this potential-
